{
    "background_story": "Poppy was a majestic toro de lidia, born and raised in the rolling hills of Spain. From a young age, she showed a fierce spirit and agility, making her a prime candidate for the novillada, a traditional bullfighting spectacle. As she matured, Poppy's strength and cunning only grew, earning her the respect of the matadors who faced her. Her most notable performance was in the Plaza de Toros, where she outmaneuvered three skilled matadors, refusing to back down. The crowd roared with admiration for the brave and agile Poppy, who had proven herself a true queen of the novillada. Though her days in the arena were numbered, Poppy's legend lived on, inspiring generations of toreros and aficionados alike.",
